## Panel 1 — Request Rate

**Type:** Time Series

```logql
sum(
  rate(
    {cmdbReference="AT56277", container="application"}
    | pattern `<_> - "<method> <path> <_>" <status> <_>`
    | __error__=""
    | pod =~ "$pod"
    [$__rate_interval]
  )
)
```

**Settings:**

- Unit → `reqps` (requests/sec)
- Legend → `Request Rate`
- Fill opacity → `10`

-----

## Panel 2 — Error Rate (4xx / 5xx)

**Type:** Time Series — add both as separate queries on the same panel

```logql
# Query A — 4xx Client Errors
sum(
  rate(
    {cmdbReference="AT56277", container="application"}
    | pattern `<_> - "<method> <path> <_>" <status> <_>`
    | status =~ "4.."
    | __error__=""
    | pod =~ "$pod"
    [$__rate_interval]
  )
)

# Query B — 5xx Server Errors
sum(
  rate(
    {cmdbReference="AT56277", container="application"}
    | pattern `<_> - "<method> <path> <_>" <status> <_>`
    | status =~ "5.."
    | __error__=""
    | pod =~ "$pod"
    [$__rate_interval]
  )
)
```

**Settings:**

- Query A color → Yellow (`#d29922`)
- Query B color → Red (`#f85149`)
- Thresholds → `0 = green`, `1 = red`

